[0.047, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[3G\u001b[48;2;55;55;55m\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m3. Key Engineering Pitfalls to Avoid\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BOv\u001b[6Gr-subdividing for Raster vs. RT: Mesh shaders perform best with 64 vertices / 64–126 triangles per meshlet, \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bwher\u001b[8Gas CLAS bu\u001b[19Glds amortize \u001b[33Gverhead best around 128 vertices / 128–256 triangles. Configure nv_cluster_builder to \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B128 vertices / 128 tri\u001b[26Gngles—it\u001b[35Ghits the\u001b[45Gweet \u001b[51Gpot where a single\u001b[70Gcluster fits inside one mesh \u001b[100Ghader workgroup and \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bke\u001b[6Gps CLAS header overhead low.\u001b[39m                                                                                     \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255mMemory Pool Fragmen\u001b[23Gation: Streamed clusters load and unlo\u001b[62Gd dynami\u001b[71Gally. Use a\u001b[83Gfixe\u001b[88G-siz\u001b[94Gblock/p\u001b[102Gg\u001b[104G allocat\u001b[113Gr \u001b[39m     \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m(\u001b[5G.g., 4 KB or 16\u001b[21GKB pages) for both your geometry slab and your CLAS output buffer rather than general-purpose \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bsub-allocation, so streaming n\u001b[34Gver stalls on\u001b[48Gdefragmentation.\u001b[39m                                                   \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255mCross-Platform\u001b[18GShader Compilation: Compile y\u001b[48Gur Mesh, Task,\u001b[63GC\u001b[65Gmpute, and Fragment shaders with Sla\u001b[102Gg (slangc -target \r\u001b[3C\u001b[1Bpirv) \u001b[11Gr glslangValidator, explicitly targeting --targe\u001b[60G-e\u001b[63Gv vulkan1.4 so SPV_NV_cluster_acceleration_structure and \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BSPV_EXT_mesh_shader validate cleanly on both Linux and Windows.\u001b[39m                                                      \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255mWhe\u001b[7Ge w\u001b[11Guld you like to dive in first for your implementation:\u00