[0.058, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[3G\u001b[48;2;55;55;55m\u001b[38;2;255;255;255mwhereas CLAS\u001b[16Gbuilds amortize overhead b\u001b[43Gst around 128 vertices / 128–256 triangles. Configur\u001b[96G nv_cluster_builder\u001b[116Gto \u001b[39m \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m128 vertices / 128 triangles—it hits the sweet spot where a single cluster fits inside one mesh shader workgroup and \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bk\u001b[5Geps CLAS header overhead\u001b[30Glow.\u001b[39m                                                                                 \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255mM\u001b[5Gmory\u001b[10GPool\u001b[15GF\u001b[17Gagmentation: Streamed clusters load and unload dynamically. Use a \u001b[84Gixed-size\u001b[94Gblock/page allocator\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B(e.g., 4 KB \u001b[16Gr 16 KB pages) for both your\u001b[45Ggeom\u001b[50Gt\u001b[52Gy slab and your CLAS output buffer rather than general-purpose \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bsub-allocation, so strea\u001b[28Ging never\u001b[38Gstalls on defragment\u001b[59Gtion.\u001b[39m                                                        \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255mCross-Platform Shader Compilation: Compile your Mesh, Task, Compute, and Fragment shaders with Sl\u001b[101Gng (slang\u001b[111G -target\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bspirv) or glslangValidator, explicitly targeting --target-env vulkan1.4 so SPV_NV_cluster_acceleration_structure and \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BSPV_EXT_mesh_shader vali\u001b[28Gat\u001b[32Gcleanly on both Linux and Wind\u001b[63Gws.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BWhere wou\u001b[13Gd you like\u001b[24Gto d\u001b[29Gve\u001b[32Gin\u001b[35Gfirst for yo\u001b[48Gr implementation:\u001b[39m                                                      \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255mOffline glTF Baking: Setting up nv_cluster_builder + nv_lod_cluster_builder in C++ to serialize your custom cluster \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bbinary format\u001b[39m                                                                             \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255mGPU Memory &\u001b[16GStreaming: Designing the page-bas\u001b[50Gd VRAM pool and CLAS \u001b[72Gdd\u001b[75Gess\u001b[80Gaching\u001b[88Gyst\u001b[92Gm\u001b[39m \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255mShader Code: Writing the Mesh Shader (VK_EXT_mesh_shader) and DAG traversal compute shader?\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255m\\\u001b[39m                                                                                                                     \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m●\u001b[39m Running bash\u001b[16G-c\u001b[19G'source\u001b[27Gscripts/lib/headless.sh;\u001b[52Gheadless…\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  $ bash -c 'source scripts/lib/hea\u001b[40Gless.sh; headless_use_lavapip\u001b[70G >/dev/null 2>&1; echo $VK_ICD_FILENAMES; \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[15C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m 2>/dev/null'\u001b[39m\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;74H\u001b[?25h"]
