[0.010, "o", "\u001b[H\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  · Ray tracing is Out in scope.md. What should this plan do about it? → RT In, KHR + MG\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;2;153;153;153m· Windows\u001b[16Gis Out in scope.md. Do\u001b[39Gs this work bring it back? → Linux only\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B· What justifies the work? AGENTS.md says to provision demonstrated gaps. → Manifest content\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;2;153;153;153m· A visibility buffer and software raster (full Nanite) don't work with MSAA. Which way? → Decide later\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39mYour answers are in: ray tracing on plain KHR, with Mega Geometry as an NVIDIA path, Linux only, driven by Manifest\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bcontent,\u001b[12Gand\u001b[16Gthe\u001b[20Ganti-aliasing\u001b[34Gchoice\u001b[41Gstill\u001b[47Gopen.\u001b[53GI'm\u001b[57Gchecking\u001b[66Gthe\u001b[70Gremaining\u001b[80Gclaims\u001b[87Gagainst\u001b[95Gthe\u001b[99Gheaders,\u001b[108Gcompiler\u001b[117Gand\r\u001b[1B  library sources.\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m · summary\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m›\u001b[3GMessage from @web-fetch (ctrl+o to expand)\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m›\u001b[3GMessage from @web-fetch (ctrl+o to expand)\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m›\u001b[3GMessage from @web-fetch (ctrl+o to\u001b[38Gexp\u001b[42Gnd)\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39mRunning bash -c 'vulkaninfo 2>/dev/null | sed -n \"/GeForc…\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  $ bash -c 'vulkaninfo 2>/dev/null | sed -n \"/GeForce RTX 5060/,/GeForce RTX 5070/p\" | grep -A16 -E \"ClusterAccelera\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1BtionStructur\u001b[19GPropertiesNV|Partitio\u001b[41GedAc\u001b[47GlerationStructureProperti\u001b[73GsNV|AccelerationStructurePropertiesKHR:\" | head \r\u001b[