[0.021, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[3G \u001b[5G(\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mvk_lod_clusters\u001b[39m, Apache-2.0)\u001b[35Gbuilds its hi\u001b[49Grarchy with a lightly modified copy of it.\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mCluster s\u001b[17G:\u001b[22m NVIDIA's animated-clusters sample recommends 64 triangles and 64 verti\u001b[90Ges. That contradicts the\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Btranscript's \"128/128 is the sweet \u001b[41Gpo\u001b[44G\". I'll measure the size rather than pick one now.\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mSampl\u001b[11G fram\u001b[17Gwork:\u001b[22m the NVIDIA samp\u001b[39Ge\u001b[41G depend on th\u001b[55Gir ow\u001b[61G \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mnvpro_core2\u001b[39m framework. They're references to read, not\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bdependencie\u001b[18Gto add.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BOne thing I haven't settled\u001b[31Gis\u001b[34Gwhether\u001b[42G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mVK_EXT_cluster_acceleration_structure\u001b[80G\u001b[39mexists\u001b[87Ganywhere:\u001b[97Gthe\u001b[101Gregistry\u001b[110Gpage\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Breturned\u001b[12G403,\u001b[17Gthough\u001b[24Git\u001b[27Gisn't\u001b[33Gon\u001b[36Gthis\u001b[41Gdriver\u001b[48Geither\u001b[55Gway.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m✻\u001b[3GBrewed for 2m 7s · done 8:38 pm\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2B\u001b[48;2;55;55;55m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m❯ \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mHow costly is ray traced reflections, and what impact would it have on the engine. Can it be offered as an optional \u001b[39m  \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mextra path for rendering and disabled when needed. I would like it if the impact isn't too strong.\u001b[39m                    \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mIs there a\u001b[14Gway to\u001b[21Ghave the mega stuff\u001b[41Gwork on AMD hard\u001b[58Gare,\u001b[63Gan\u001b[66Gequivalent API / SDK? If not then it needs t\u001b[111G be \u001b[39m    \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255mop\u001b[6Giona