[0.003, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[3G-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mThe same bytes every run.\u001b[31G\u001b[22mA\u001b[33Gpinned\u001b[40Gmeshoptimizer\u001b[54Gand\u001b[58Gfixed\u001b[64Ginputs\u001b[71Ggive\u001b[76Gthe\u001b[80Gsame\u001b[85Ghierarchy\u001b[95Geach\u001b[100Gtime,\u001b[106Gwhich\u001b[112Gis\u001b[115Gwhat\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B  the reference frames need.\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mSimulation determinism is J12's question, not this plan's.\u001b[64G\u001b[22mIf \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mphysics\u001b[75G\u001b[39mreads collision\u001b[91Gmeshes from it,\u001b[107GJ12\u001b[111Gdecides\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B \u001b[5Gthen whether the module gets the \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mDETERMINISTIC\u001b[39m flag.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mCost to a game with no dense content:\u001b[22m a small MIT library\u001b[63Gcompiled\u001b[72Gin.\u001b[76GNothing\u001b[84Gruns\u001b[89Gunless\u001b[96Ga\u001b[98Gmodel\u001b[104Gloads.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BDo you want th\u001b[19Gnew \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mgeometry\u001b[32G\u001b[39mmodule,\u001b[40Gor\u001b[43Gone\u001b[47Gof\u001b[50Gthe\u001b[54Gother\u001b[60Goptions?\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m✻\u001b[3GCrunched for 29s · done 8:58 pm\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[48;2;55;55;55m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m❯ \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mNew geometry module, go with your recommendation We will be using a cook stage in the asset pipeline, so all gltf \u001b[39m    \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255massets will be cooked into a performant and suitable format for consumption by the engine. That may also be gltf if \u001b[39m  \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mit supports everything we need. I am leaning towards having a sidecar outside the game repo for all the game assets \u001b[39m  \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mthat the artists author. A small command line daemon tool would watch that folder for file changes, and cook the \u001b[39m     \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255massets into the format the engine requires, moving them into an asset folder inside the game repo at that point, that\u001b[39m \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mmirrors the structure of the original asset folder. This keeps massive source assets out of the game asset repo. A \u001b[39m   \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255myaml file with matching name of the source asset (sidecar) would be able to override default processing settings so \u001b[39m  \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255massets can have specific cook parameters set for them e.g. big-ship.gltf might have big-ship.gltf.yaml as it's \u001b[39m       \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255msidecar.\u001b[39m                                                                                                              \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;215;119;87m✻\u001b[3GJitterbugging\u001b[38;2;235;159;127m…\u001b[38;2;215;119;87m \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;136;136;136m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── jettison-0030 ─\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m❯ \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[38C\u001b[3B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m · esc to interrupt · ← 1 agent\u001b[39m\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
