[0.182, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[6G\u001b[2m 533 \u001b[12G\u001b[22m###\u001b[16GJ48.\u001b[21GMega\u001b[26GGeometry\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 534 \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[22m   \u001b[38;2;220;90;90m\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m 535 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m- **Delivers.** CLAS per loaded meshlet, built as pages arrive; per-instance bottom-level structures  \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m 536 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  from the current cut; the alignments and limits from the device's properties;                       \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;2;220;90;90m\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m 537 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  `scripts/mega-geometry-check.sh`, which draws the benchmark scene on the 5060 Ti offscreen with     \u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B   \u001b[38;2;220;90;90m\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m 538 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  and without it and compares the frames.                                                             \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m 539 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m- **Exit criterion.** The check script's frames agree within the reference views' fuzz, with          \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;2;220;90;90m\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m 540 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  shadows that match the raster's level of detail; the build times recorded. The gate is unaffected:  \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 535 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m- **Delivers.** The `meshlet-traverse` pass and its two cuts; CLAS per loaded meshlet, built as       \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m   \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 536 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  pages arrive; per-instance bottom-level structures from the rays' cut; the alignments, limits and   \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 537 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  scratch sizes from the device's properties, all within the geometry budget; a debug mode feeding    \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 538 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  the KHR builder the same cut as triangles; `scripts/mega-geometry-check.sh`, which draws the        \u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B   \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 539 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  benchmark scene on the 5060 Ti offscreen with each builder and compares the frames.                 \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 540 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m- **Exit criterion.** With the same cut, the two builders' frames agree within the reference views'   \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m   \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 541 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  fuzz; a view of a dense silhouette under a low sun shows neither acne nor a leak at the raster's    \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 542 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  level of detail; build times and memory recorded. The gate is unaffected:                           \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m     \u001b[2m 543 \u001b[22m   lavapipe lacks the extension.\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B     \u001b[2m 544 \u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B     \u001b[2m 545 \u001b[22m ### J49. Temporal foundation and glossy reflections\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[2B\u001b[38;2;233;154;122mMetamorphosing…\u001b[39m\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
