[0.020, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m     \u001b[22m the device table, so a\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 374 \u001b[22m   future `EXT` or `KHR` cluster extension is a local change.\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 375 \u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;78;186;101m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39m\u001b[1mUpdate\u001b[22m(docs/dense-geometry-and-ray-tracing.md)\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  \u001b[39mAdded\u001b[12G\u001b[1m4\u001b[14G\u001b[22mlines, removed \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m line\u001b[K\r\u001b[7C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m36\u001b[12G\u001b[22m \u001b[14G`clust\u001b[21Grlod.h`; attributes quantised. The co\u001b[59Gked GLB\u001b[67Gkeeps the\u001b[77Gnodes, sk\u001b[88Gs,\u001b[91Gclips an\u001b[101Gextras the\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 237 \u001b[14G\u001b[22mrig\u001b[18Gand\u001b[22Gdocks\u001b[28Gread,\u001b[34Gand\u001b[38Gis\u001b[41Gwritten\u001b[49Gby\u001b[52Gfastgltf.\r\u001b[1B \u001b[3G   \u001b[2m 238 \u001b[22m - **Textur\u001b[23Gs.** The images a model's materials\u001b[59Gname,\u001b[65Gand\u001b[69Gloose\u001b[75Gimages,\u001b[83Gbecome\u001b[90GKTX\u001b[94G2\u001b[96Gwith\u001b[101Gthe\u001b[105Gimport\r\u001b[1B     \u001b[38;2;220;90;90m\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m 239 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  script's settings (UASTC for colour and normal maps), through libktx's encoder.                     \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 239 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  script's settings (UASTC for colour and normal maps), through libktx's encoder.\u001b[48;2;4;71;0m A cooked GLB\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m        \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 240 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  names them through `KHR_texture_basisu`, with no PNG fallback, so the reader enables that           \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 241 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  extension too, the model loader takes the extension's image index, and the material cache decodes   \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 242 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  KTX 2 through `Texture`'s existing reader instead of `DecodeImage` (stb_image).                     \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[2m 243 \u001b[22m - **Formats.** No version numbers or migrations until player testing\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 244 \u001b[22m   ([\u001b[38;2;230;219;116mformats in place\u001b[39m](decisions.md#persistence)): a format change cooks everything again.\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 245 \u001b[22m - **The engine's own content** (`source/test/content`) is cooked by CMake into the build tree, as\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;78;186;101m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39m\u001b[1mUpdate\u001b[22m(docs/dense-geometry-and-ray-tracing.md)\u001b[50G\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  \u001b[39mAdded\u001b[12G\u001b[1m2\u001b[14G\u001b[22mlines, removed \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m line \u001b[37G     \u001b[43G  \u001b[46G \u001b[76G\u001b[K\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
[0.372, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;78;186;101m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39m\u001b[1mUpdate\u001b[22m(docs/dense-geometry-and-ray-tracing.md)\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  \u001b[39mAdded\u001b[12G\u001b[1m2\u001b[14G\u001b[22mlines,\u001b[21Gremoved \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m line\u001b[36G\u001b[K\r\u001b[7C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m68\u001b[14G\u001b[22minstance's\u001b[25Ghierarchy\u001b[35Gand\u001b[39Gwrites\u001b[46Gtwo\u001b[50Gcuts:\u001b[56Gthe\u001b[60Graster's,\u001b[70Gwhich\u001b[76Gthe\u001b[80Gtask\u001b[85Gshaders\u001b[93Gthen\u001b[98Gcull,\u001b[104Gand\u001b[108Gthe\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 369 \u001b[14G\u001b[22mrays',\u001b[21Gfor\u001b[25Gevery\u001b[31Ginstance\u001b[40Gin\u001b[43Gthe\u001b[47Gray-tracing\u001b[59Grange\u001b[65Gwith\u001b[70Gno\u001b[73Gfrustum\u001b[81Gor\u001b[84Gocclusion\u001b[94Gtest,\u001b[100Gsince\r\u001b[1B \u001b[3G   \u001b[2m 370 \u001b[22m   geometry \u001b[24Gff screen or hidden still\u001b[50Gcasts\u001b[56Gshadows\u001b[64Gand\u001b[68Gshows\u001b[74Gin\u001b[77Greflections.\u001b[90GThe\u001b[94Grays'\u001b[100Gcut\u001b[104Gmay\u001b[108Gbe\r\u001b[1B     \u001b[38;2;220;90;90m\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m 371 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  coarser, by a setting. Each instance's bottom-level structure is built from the rays' cut, after    \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 371 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  coarser, by a setting. Both cuts request missing pages and stamp the pages they use, as             \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 372 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  [\u001b[38;2;230;219;116mstreaming\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m](#the-frame) describes. Each instance's bottom-level structure is built from the rays' cu\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mt, after                                                                                              \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[2m 373 \u001b[22m   a barrier, so ray tracing sees close to what the raster draws. The capability is one builder behind\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m     \u001b[22m the device table, so a\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 374 \u001b[22m   future `EXT` or `KHR` cluster extension is a local change.\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 375 \u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;78;186;101m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39m\u001b[1mUpdate\u001b[22m(docs/dense-geometry-and-ray-tracing.md)\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  \u001b[39mAdded\u001b[12G\u001b[1m4\u001b[14G\u001b[22mlines, removed \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m line\u001b[K\r\u001b[7C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m36\u001b[12G\u001b[22m \u001b[14G`clust\u001b[21Grlod.h`; attributes quantised. The co\u001b[59Gked GLB\u001b[67Gkeeps the\u001b[77Gnodes, sk\u001b[88Gs,\u001b[91Gclips an\u001b[101Gextras the\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 237 \u001b[14G\u001b[22mrig\u001b[18Gand\u001b[22Gdocks\u001b[28Gread,\u001b[34Gand\u001b[38Gis\u001b[41Gwritten\u001b[49Gby\u001b[52Gfastgltf.\r\u001b[1B \u001b[3G   \u001b[2m 238 \u001b[22m - **Textur\u001b[23Gs.** The images a model's materials\u001b[59Gname,\u001b[65Gand\u001b[69Gloose\u001b[75Gimages,\u001b[83Gbecome\u001b[90GKTX\u001b[94G2\u001b[96Gwith\u001b[101Gthe\u001b[105Gimport\r\u001b[1B     \u001b[38;2;220;90;90m\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m 239 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  script's settings (UASTC for colo\u001b[76Glibktx's encoder.                     \u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
[0.404, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[1B \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 326 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  read a frame in flight later, and stamps each page it used with the frame. The I/O worker reads     \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 327 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  the wanted pages, decodes them and uploads through a staging ring into a pool of fixed-size pages;  \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 328 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  the least recently used are evicted. Demand comes from every cut: the raster's, and with            \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 329 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  [\u001b[38;2;230;219;116mJ48\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m](roadmap.md#j48) the rays' as well, so geometry seen only in a reflection or a shadow is       \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 330 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  requested and kept like anything on screen. The coarsest levels are always loaded, so every model   \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 331 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  always draws something.                                                                             \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[2m 332 \u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 333 \u001b[22m ### Ray tracing\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 334 \u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;78;186;101m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39m\u001b[1mUpdate\u001b[22m(docs/dense-geometry-and-ray-tracing.md)\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  \u001b[39mAdded\u001b[12G\u001b[1m2\u001b[14G\u001b[22mlines,\u001b[21Gremoved \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m line\u001b[36G\u001b[K\r\u001b[7C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m68\u001b[14G\u001b[22minstance's\u001b[25Ghierarchy\u001b[35Gand\u001b[39Gwrites\u001b[46Gtwo\u001b[50Gcuts:\u001b[56Gthe\u001b[60Graster's,\u001b[70Gwhich\u001b[76Gthe\u001b[80Gtask\u001b[85Gshaders\u001b[93Gthen\u001b[98Gcull,\u001b[104Gand\u001b[108Gthe\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 369 \u001b[14G\u001b[22mrays',\u001b[21Gfor\u001b[25Gevery\u001b[31Ginstance\u001b[40Gin\u001b[43Gthe\u001b[47Gray-tracing\u001b[59Grange\u001b[65Gwith\u001b[70Gno\u001b[73Gfrustum\u001b[81Gor\u001b[84Gocclusion\u001b[94Gtest,\u001b[100Gsince\r\u001b[1B \u001b[3G   \u001b[2m 370 \u001b[22m   geometry \u001b[24Gff screen or hidden still\u001b[50Gcasts\u001b[56Gshadows\u001b[64Gand\u001b[68Gshows\u001b[74Gin\u001b[77Greflections.\u001b[90GThe\u001b[94Grays'\u001b[100Gcut\u001b[104Gmay\u001b[108Gbe\r\u001b[1B     \u001b[38;2;220;90;90m\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m 371 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  coarser, by a setting. Each instance's bottom-level structure is built from the rays' cut, after    \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 371 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  coarser, by a setting. Both cuts request missing pages and stamp the pages they use, as             \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 372 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  [\u001b[38;2;230;219;116mstreaming\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m](#the-frame) describes. Each instance's bottom-level structure is built from the rays' cu\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mt, after                                                                                              \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[2m 373 \u001b[22m   a barrier, so ray tracing sees cl\u001b[76G The capability is one builder behind\u001b[K\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
