[0.342, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[1B     \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 326 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  read a frame in flight later, and stamps each page it used with the frame. The I/O worker reads     \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 327 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  the wanted pages, decodes them and uploads through a staging ring into a pool of fixed-size pages;  \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 328 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  the least recently used are evicted. Demand comes from every cut: the raster's, and with            \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 329 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  [\u001b[38;2;230;219;116mJ48\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m](roadmap.md#j48) the rays' as well, so geometry seen only in a reflection or a shadow is       \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 330 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  requested and kept like anything on screen. The coarsest levels are always loaded, so every model   \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 331 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  always draws something.                                                                             \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[2m 332 \u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 333 \u001b[22m ### Ray tracing\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 334 \u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;78;186;101m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39m\u001b[1mUpdate\u001b[22m(docs/dense-geometry-and-ray-tracing.md)\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  \u001b[39mAdded \u001b[1m2\u001b[22m lines, removed \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m line\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 368 \u001b[22m   instance's hierarchy and writes two cuts: the raster's, which the task shaders then cull, and the\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 369 \u001b[22m   rays', for every instance in the ray-tracing range with no frustum or occlusion test, since\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 370 \u001b[22m   geometry off screen or hidden still casts shadows and shows in reflections. The rays' cut may be\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m 371 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  coarser, by a setting. Each instance's bottom-level structure is built from the rays' cut, after    \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 371 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  coarser, by a setting. Both cuts request missing pages and stamp the pages they use, as             \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 372 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  [\u001b[38;2;230;219;116mstreaming\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m](#the-frame) describes. Each instance's bottom-level structure is built from the rays' cu\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mt, after                                                                                              \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[2m 373 \u001b[14G\u001b[22ma\u001b[16Gbarrier,\u001b[25Gso\u001b[28Gray\u001b[32Gtracing\u001b[40Gsees\u001b[45Gcl\u001b[77GThe\u001b[81Gcapability\u001b[92Gis\u001b[95Gone\u001b[99Gbuilder\u001b[107Gbehind\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
