[0.001, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;78;186;101m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39m\u001b[1mUpdate\u001b[22m(docs/dense-geometry-and-ray-tracing.md)\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  \u001b[39mAdded \u001b[1m2\u001b[22m lines, removed \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m line\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 368 \u001b[22m   instance's hierarchy and writes two cuts: the raster's, which the task shaders then cull, and the\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 369 \u001b[22m   rays', for every instance in the ray-tracing range with no frustum or occlusion test, since\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 370 \u001b[22m   geometry off screen or hidden still casts shadows and shows in reflections. The rays' cut may be\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m 371 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  coarser, by a setting. Each instance's bottom-level structure is built from the rays' cut, after    \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 371 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  coarser, by a setting. Both cuts request missing pages and stamp the pages they use, as             \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 372 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  [\u001b[38;2;230;219;116mstreaming\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m](#the-frame) describes. Each instance's bottom-level structure is built from the rays' cu\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m     +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mt, after                                                                                              \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[2m 373 \u001b[14G\u001b[22ma\u001b[16Gbarrier,\u001b[25Gso\u001b[28Gray\u001b[32Gtracing\u001b[40Gsees\u001b[45Gclose\u001b[51Gto\u001b[54Gwhat\u001b[59Gthe\u001b[63Graster\u001b[70Gdraws.\u001b[77GThe\u001b[81Gcapability\u001b[92Gis\u001b[95Gone\u001b[99Gbuilder\u001b[107Gbehind\r\u001b[1B \u001b[3G   \u001b[2m     \u001b[22m the device table, so a\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B     \u001b[2m 374 \u001b[12G\u001b[22m \u001b[14Gfuture\u001b[21G`EXT` or `KHR`\u001b[36Gcluster\u001b[44Gextension\u001b[54Gis\u001b[57Ga\u001b[59Glocal\u001b[65Gchange.\r\u001b[7C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m75\u001b[14G\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;78;186;101m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39m\u001b[1mUpdate\u001b[22m(docs/dense-ge\u001b[24Gmetry-and-ray-tracing.md)\u001b[50G\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  \u001b[39mAdded \u001b[1m4\u001b[22m lines, removed \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m line\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 236 \u001b[22m   `clusterlod.h`; attributes quantised. The cooked GLB keeps the nodes, skins, clips and extras the\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 237 \u001b[22m   rig and docks read, and is written by fastgltf.\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 238 \u001b[22m - **Textures.** The images a model's materials name, and loose images, become KTX 2 with the import\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m 239 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  script's settings (UASTC for colo\u001b[76Glibktx's encoder.                     \u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
