\u001b[22m \u001b[14Gmeshlet file beside it\u001b[37Gdraws\u001b[43Gon\u001b[46Gthe\u001b[50Gindexed\u001b[58Gpath,\u001b[64Gso\u001b[67Gan\u001b[70Guncooked\u001b[79GglTF\u001b[84Gkeeps\u001b[90Gworking,\u001b[99Gwith\u001b[104Ga\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;78;186;101m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39m\u001b[1mUpdate\u001b[22m(docs/dense-ge\u001b[24Gmetry-and-ray-tracing.md)\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  \u001b[39mAdded\u001b[12G\u001b[1m2\u001b[14G\u001b[22mlines,\u001b[21Gremoved\u001b[29G\u001b[1m2\u001b[22m lines\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 452 \u001b[22m - **Exit criterion.** The `geometry` suite proves the levels' errors grow and the cook's output is\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 453 \u001b[22m   the same bytes twice; the cook suite cooks a fixture tree, skips what is unchanged, deletes what\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 454 \u001b[22m   lost its source, and cooks a model again when only its buffer, an image or `cook.yaml` changed;\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m 455 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  the animation suite reads a cooked skinned fixture with its joints, clips and poses intact; \u001b[48;2;92;2;0mthe\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m     \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m 456 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  render test draws cooked models; a reference view shows a generated asteroid                        \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 455 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  the animation suite reads a cooked skinned fixture with its joints, clips and poses intact; \u001b[48;2;4;71;0ma\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m       \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 456 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  \u001b[48;2;4;71;0mreference view draws a cooked tex\u001b[75Gase colour; the \u001b[48;2;2;40;0mrender test draws cooke\u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
