[0.004, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[48;2;55;55;55m  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255msingle std430 SSBO indexed by shapeIndex * vertexCount + gl_VertexIndex. Pass current weights via a UBO/SSBO array.\u001b[39m   \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mMorph Animations    channel.target.path == \"weights\"    Sample a flat float[] keyframe track (stride = number of \u001b[39m     \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mshape keys) alongside your existing translation/rotation/scale channels.\u001b[39m                                              \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mBlend Spaces    Multiple glTF Animation clips    Create an engine-side asset/JSON file that maps glTF clip names to \u001b[39m  \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255m(X, Y) coordinates, then evaluate and blend Pose structs on the CPU.\u001b[39m                                                  \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255m3. Starter Prompt for Claude Code (Blend Shapes)\u001b[39m                                                                      \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mYou can hand this directly to Claude Code to scaffold the first milestone:\u001b[39m                                            \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255m*\"Inspect our glTF loader and Vulkan mesh/shader pipeline. I want to add support for glTF morph targets (blend \u001b[39m       \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mshapes) authored in Blender.\u001b[39m                                                                                          \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mUpdate\u001b[10Gthe\u001b[14GglTF loader to parse primitive.targets (POSITION and NORMAL deltas), default mesh.weights, and \r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mmesh.extras[\"targetNames\"].\u001b[39m                                                                                           \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mPack the morph deltas into a Vulkan Storage Buffer (SSBO) per mesh.\u001b[39m                                                   \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mUpdate our skinned vertex shader to read a weights array from a UBO/SSBO and apply active morph target deltas to the \u001b[39m \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mvertex position and normal BEFORE applying skeletal skinning matrices.\u001b[39m                                                \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mExpose the weights on the mesh component so I can test them with sliders.\"*\u001b[39m                                           \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mIf you'd like to keep building this out, let me know:\u001b[39m                                                                 \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mWhich glTF library your codebase uses (fastgltf, tinygltf, or cgltf)\u001b[39m                                                  \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mWhether you want a Claude Code prompt for the 2D blend space next\u001b[39m                                                     \r\u001b[1B                                                                                                                        \r\u001b[2B\u001b[49m\u001b[38;2;215;119;87m✻\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;215;119;87mPouncing… \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;136;136;136m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── jettison-0030 ─\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m❯ \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[3B\u001b[38;2;255;193;7m⏵⏵ auto mode on\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
