[0.809, "o", "\u001b[H\r\u001b[14C\u001b[7B ☒ Face drivers \u001b[48;2;177;185;249m\u001b[38;2;0;0;0m ☐ Root motion \r\u001b[2B\u001b[39m\u001b[49m\u001b[2m│\u001b[22m \u001b[38;2;255;255;255m\u001b[1mAnimation\u001b[13Gis pr\u001b[19Gsentation only: it never moves the simulation. How should locomotion work?\r\u001b[2B\u001b[22m\u001b[38;2;177;185;249m❯\u001b[6GIn place (Recommended)\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mThe simulation m\u001b[23Gves the char\u001b[36Gcter. The blen\u001b[52Gspace is\u001b[62Ghosen by its velocity and plays at a rate matched to its \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m  \u001b[6G\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mspeed, so feet slide little. The existing decision stands.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B2.\u001b[6G\u001b[39mRoot motion\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B  \u001b[6G\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mClips move the character. This reverses the presentation-only decision and puts animation in the simulation, \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bdeterministic and \u001b[25Geplayed.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m3\u001b[6G\u001b[39mRoot motion as data\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mThe cook pulls each clip's root speed out as data, which the game's movement code can read to set its speeds. \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m   \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mAnimation still \u001b[23Gever moves the simulation.\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m \u001b[3G\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m4. Type something.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[2B\u001b[39m5\r\u001b[47C\u001b[2B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mEsc to\u001b[55Gcancel\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[27;1H\u001b[12;1H"]
