[0.004, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  · Who needs blend shapes and blend spaces first? The engine's rule is an acceptance test in an independent engine \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bconsumer and in Manifest, and today no consumer has characters. → Manifest, A future game, Engine test content, \r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mMechanical morphs\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B   \u001b[38;2;153;153;153m· What drives a face's shape weights? → Authored clips, Game code, Lip sync\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B· Animation is presentation only: it never moves the simulation. How should locomotion work? → In place \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m   \u001b[38;2;153;153;153m(Recommended)\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m· How are clips, blend spaces and faces combined on one character? → Components (Recommended)\r\u001b[1B────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\u001b[1B← \u001b[48;2;177;185;249m\u001b[38;2;0;0;0m ☐ Manifest use \u001b[39m\u001b[49m ☐ Lip sync  ☐\u001b[34GBlend spaces \u001b[48G☐ IK  ✔ Submit  →\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m\u001b[1mWhat will Manifest's characters do? This sets what the engine must prove first.\r\u001b[1B\u001b[22m\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;177;185;249m❯\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;153;153;153m1.\u001b[39m [ ] \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mPortraits\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B    \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mFaces in\u001b[19Gdialogue or tra\u001b[35Ge panels:\u001b[46Glo\u001b[49Ge up, talking, expressions. No walking.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m2.\u001b[6G\u001b[39m[ ] Walk interiors\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B    \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mPeople walking in stations and \u001b[42Ghips, with lo\u001b[56Gomotion blend spaces, seen at mid range.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B3.\u001b[6G\u001b[39m[ ] Seated pilots\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B    \