[1.067, "o", "\u001b[H\r\u001b[8B←  ☒ Manifest use \u001b[48;2;177;185;249m\u001b[38;2;0;0;0m ☐ Lip sync \r\u001b[2B\u001b[49m\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m\u001b[1mHow shou\u001b[10Gd lip sync be made?\u001b[22m\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2B\u001b[38;2;177;185;249m❯\u001b[6GAt cook time (Recommended)\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mThe cook analyses each dialogue line's\u001b[45Gaudio\u001b[51Goffline a\u001b[61Gd writes a clip\u001b[77Gof\u001b[80Gmouth-shape weights beside it. Nothing \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m  \u001b[6G\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mextra at runtime, and the result can be checked like any clip. The tool and its licence are to be verified.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B2.\u001b[6G\u001b[39mRuntime, volume\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B  \u001b[6G\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mThe jaw opens with the playing sound's loudness. Cheap and crude; works for any sound, procedural voices too.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B3.\u001b[6G\u001b[39mRuntime, phonemes\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B  \u001b[6G\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mMouth shapes from live speech analysis. Heavy, and it needs a model or library at runtime.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B4.\u001b[6G\u001b[39mBoth cook and volume\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B   \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mCook-time clips for authored dialogue, with volume as the fallback for anything without one.\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m \u001b[3G\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m5. Type something.\r\u001b[47C\u001b[4BEsc to\u001b[55Gcancel\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[27;1H\u001b[13;1H"]
