[0.004, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[6G\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m· How shoul\u001b[19Glip sync be m\u001b[33Gde? → At\u001b[42Gc\u001b[44Gok time (Recommended)\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m· W\u001b[10Gich b\u001b[16Gend spaces, and how are gaits kept in step? → 1D+2D, markers (Rec.)\r\u001b[7C\u001b[1BInverse kinemati\u001b[25Gs is Out in scope today. What\u001b[55Gabout feet and hands?\u001b[77G→ Two-bone IK, later\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mRan \u001b[1m8\u001b[22m shell commands \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39mRhubarb\u001b[11GLip\u001b[15GSync\u001b[20Gchecked\u001b[28Gout:\u001b[33Git's\u001b[38GMIT-licensed\u001b[51Gwith\u001b[56Gpermissive\u001b[67Gdependencies,\u001b[81Gstill\u001b[87Gmaintained,\u001b[99Gand\u001b[103Ghas\u001b[107Ga\u001b[109GLinux\u001b[115Gbuild.\r\u001b[1B \u001b[3GIt\u001b[6G wor\u001b[12Grecognition only works\u001b[35Gin\u001b[38GEnglish,\u001b[47Gso\u001b[50Gfor\u001b[54GFrench,\u001b[62GGerman\u001b[69Gand\u001b[73GJapanese\u001b[82Git\u001b[85Gwould\u001b[91Gfall\u001b[96Gback\u001b[101Gto\u001b[104Ga\u001b[106Gless\u001b[111Gprecise\r\u001b[1B  language-independent mode, and it fits as an external program the cook runs rather than a linked library.\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m · summary\r\u001b[1B────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\u001b[1B← \u001b[48;2;177;185;249m\u001b[38;2;0;0;0m ☐ Deform pass \u001b[39m\u001b[49m ☐ Mesh nodes  ☐ Face shading  ☐ Schedule  ✔ Submit\u001b[71G→\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[2m│\u001b[3G\u001b[22m\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m\u001b[1mWhere should morphing and skinning run? J42 already plans a compute pass that skins once per frame, which ray tracing \r\u001b[1B\u001b[22m\u001b[39m\u001b[2m│\u001b[3G\u001b[22m\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m\u001b[1mneeds.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[22m\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;177;185;249m❯\u001b[3G\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m1.\u001b[6G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mCompute, brought forward (Rec.)\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mOne compute pass per frame morphs, then skins, each animated instance into its own vertex buffer, which every pass \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m   \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mreads. It becomes a stage of this track, and J42 reuses it rather than building it.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m2.\u001b[39m Vert\u001b[11Gx shad\u001b[18Gr\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mMorph in the vertex shader beside today's skinning. Less work now, but repeated in every pass (prepass, opaque, \r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;2;153;153;153meach cascade),\u001b[21Gand J\u001b[27G2 still has to build the compute pass.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B3. Type something.\r\u001b[1B────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m  4.\u001b[6GChat\u001b[11Gabout\u001b[17Gthis\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mEnter to select · Tab/Arrow keys to navigate · Esc to cancel\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;136;136;136m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── jettison-0030 ─\u001b[39m\u001b[27;1H\u001b[16;1H"]
