[0.005, "o", "\u001b[H\r\u001b[17C\u001b[10B ☒ Mesh nodes \u001b[48;2;177;185;249m\u001b[38;2;0;0;0m ☐ Face shading \r\u001b[2C\u001b[2B\u001b[49m\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m\u001b[1mPort\u001b[8Gaits put faces close up. Scope\u001b[39Ghas skin,\u001b[49Ghair and\u001b[58Gfac\u001b[62Gs\u001b[64GOut. What shading comes\u001b[88Gwith this?\u001b[22m\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;177;185;249m❯\u001b[3G\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m1.\u001b[6G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mStays Out\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m \u001b[3G  \u001b[6G\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mFaces lit by the existing PBR materials. Stylised or helmeted characters look fine; realistic skin reads as \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bplastic.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m2.\u001b[6G\u001b[39mSkin and eyes\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B  \u001b[6G\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mA skin material with cheap subsurface scattering, and an eye material (refraction, wet highlight). Hair stays Out.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B3.\u001b[6G\u001b[39mSkin, eyes, hair\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B   \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mHair\u001b[11Gcards with alpha too, which brings alpha-tested geometry (any-hit shaders in the ray-tracing plan).\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m  \u001b[38;2;153;153;153m4. Type something.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m5.\u001b[6GChat\u001b[11Gabout\u001b[17Gthis\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mEnter to select · Tab/Arrow keys to navigate · Esc to cancel\u001b[39m\u001b[27;1H\u001b[15;1H"]
