[0.007, "o", "\u001b[H\u001b[6G\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mconsumer and in Manifest, and today no consumer has characters. → Manifest, A future game, Engine test content, \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1BMechanical morphs\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m   \u001b[38;2;153;153;153m· What drives a face's shape weights? → Authored clips, Game code, Lip sync\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B· Animation is presentation only: it never moves the simulation. How should locomotion work? → In place \r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;2;153;153;153m(Recommended)\u001b[20G\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B   \u001b[38;2;153;153;153m· How are clips, blend spaces and faces combined on one character? → Components (Recommended)\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39mAnswered\u001b[12GClaude's\u001b[21Gquestions:\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  · What will Manifest's characters do? This sets what the engine must prove first. → Portraits, Walk interiors, \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B \u001b[4G \u001b[6G\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mSeated pilots\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m· How should lip sync be made? → At cook time (Recommended)\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;2;153;153;153m· Which blend spaces, and how are gaits kept in step? → 1D+2D, markers (Rec.)\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B· Inverse kinematics is Out in scope today. What about feet and hands? → Two-bone IK, later\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mRan \u001b[1m8\u001b[22m shell commands \r\u001b[3C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m●\u001b[39m Rhubarb Lip Sync ch\u001b[23Gcked out: it's MIT-lic\u001b[46Gnsed with\u001b[56Gp\u001b[58Grmissive\u001b[67Gdependencies, still maintained,\u001b[99Gand has a Linux build.\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B Its w\u001b[9Grd recogn\u001b[19Gtion on\u001b[27Gy works\u001b[35Gin\u001b[38GEnglish,\u001b[47Gso\u001b[50Gfor\u001b[54GFrench,\u001b[62GGerman\u001b[69Gan