[0.100, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39mAn\u001b[6Gwere\u001b[12GClaude's questions:\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  · Where should morphing and skinning run? J42 already plans a compute pass that skins once per frame, which r\u001b[116Gy \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Btracing needs. → Compute, brought forward (Rec.)\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;2;153;153;153m· The rig loader refuses a model with more than one mesh node. Characters usually have several (body, eyes, teeth, \r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mclothing). Lift the limit? → Several\u001b[43Gmeshes (Rec.)\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m· Portraits put faces close up. Scope has\u001b[48Gskin, hair and faces Out. What shading comes with this? → Skin, eyes, \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bhair\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m· When should \u001b[21Ghis track be built, against the dense geometry and ray tracing track (J36 to J50)? → After J37 \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B(Rec.)\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39mAnswered Claude's questions:\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  · Hair with skin and eyes: how is hair made? Today the engine has no alpha-tested geometry, and the ray-tracing \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bplan relies on that. → Alpha-tested cards (Rec.)\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;2;153;153;153m· Skin needs light to scatter under the surface. Which approach? → Pre-integrated (Rec.)\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m     \u001b[8G\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mDo faces follow a naming\u001b[33Gstandard for shape keys? → ARKit 52 (Rec.)\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m· Seat\u001b[13Gd pil\u001b[19Gts and portraits look at things. Should heads and eyes follow a target? → With IK later\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39mThe interview answers are in and turned into planned work for hair, skin\u001b[76Gand\u001b[80Geyes,\u001b[86Gwhich\u001b[92Gchanges\u001b[100Gsome\u001b[105Gray-tracing\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bassumptions. I'm verifying the remaining facts against primary sources before writing anything.\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m · summary\r\u001b[2B\u001b[38;2;215;119;87m✻\u001b[3GPouncing… \u001b[40G\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mthought for 48s)\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
